  "annotations": [
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "GPT5 Story failed to block the attacking Thraben Inspector (1/2) with Kami of Ancient Law (2/2). Kami would have killed the Inspector and survived at 2/1 remaining toughness. This was a free profitable block that removes the opponent's creature.",
      "action_taken": "No response (timed out), did not block — took 1 damage and let Thraben Inspector survive.",
      "better_line": "Block Thraben Inspector with Kami of Ancient Law. Kami kills the Inspector and survives, removing the opponent's creature for free.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 60,
      "player": "GPT5 Story",
      "decision_index": 24,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Cast Drag Under before playing the Plains land drop. Since Drag Under draws a card, playing the land first preserves more flexibility: after resolving Drag Under, having 4 lands means they could leave Thriving Isle untapped (for blue mana) instead of just the new Plains (white only), allowing them to potentially cast Spectral Sailor or hold up blue mana based on what they draw.",
      "action_taken": "Cast Drag Under before playing Plains land",
      "better_line": "Play Plains first, then cast Drag Under using Island + original Plains + Thriving Isle, keeping the new Plains or Thriving Isle untapped for more flexible mana after seeing the drawn card.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 108,
      "player": "GPT5 Story",
      "decision_index": 38,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Opponent has zero creatures on the battlefield and all lands are tapped, meaning there are no blockers and no instant-speed interaction possible. Attacking with only Merfolk Pupil instead of both creatures leaves 1 free damage on the table.",
      "action_taken": "Attacked with only Merfolk Pupil (1 damage)",
      "better_line": "Attack with all creatures (Merfolk Pupil and Gideon's Lawkeeper) for 2 damage, since the opponent has no creatures and all lands are tapped. Lawkeeper will untap next turn and be available for its tap ability then.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 118,
      "player": "GPT5 Story",
      "decision_index": 43,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Young Pyromancer (2/1) trades with Merfolk Pupil (1/1) — both die since Young Pyromancer only has 1 toughness. Young Pyromancer is a high-value card that generates tokens from future instants/sorceries, while Merfolk Pupil is just a 1/1 with its ETB already used. Saving 1 damage at 17 life is not worth sacrificing Young Pyromancer. Additionally, putting Merfolk Pupil in the graveyard gives the opponent access to its card filtering ability.",
      "action_taken": "Blocked Merfolk Pupil with Young Pyromancer, trading both creatures",
      "better_line": "Don't block — take the 1 damage and preserve Young Pyromancer for future token generation value",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 143,
      "player": "MiniMx Worrier",
      "decision_index": 52,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
